      "originalText": "Day 22 - 4 layered architecture:\nIn this class sir taught 4 layered architecutre\nusing authentication setup.\n4 layered architecture means presentation layer,\nbusiness logic layer, data fetching layer, and data\nmanaging layer. in the form of folder for ui, hook, \napi, state. \nI created authentication set up with 4 layerd\narchitecture. First i create features folder inside\ni create auth, cart, product, and orders. inside this \nall folder i created another 4 folder that is\nui, hook, api, and state. then in auth folder inside\ni do all work in this class. \nin auth inside ui folder i create component and page\nfolder inside page folder i created login and \nregister page, and wrote ui of register and login page. \nthen inside src folder i created app folder inside app\ni created store.jsx for set up redux store, then i created\ninsdie app layouts folder inside layout i created\nauthlayout, mainlayout inside this layout i wrote outlet\nfor acception another route or children.\nin src folder i create another config folder inside that\nfolder i created api.jsx file inside i wrote axios \ninstance for api call. after that on auth folder inside\napi folder i created Authapi.jsx file then inside \ni create function loginUserApi inside I used post api and pass\n/auth/login and creditial like this.\nexport const loginUserApi = async (credential) => {\n  try {\n    let res = await api.post(\"/auth/login\", credential);\n    localStorage.setItem(\"accessToken\", res.data.accessToken);\n    return res.data;\n  } catch (error) {\n    console.log(\"Api errors\", error);\n  }\n};\n\nand call this loginUserApi function inside auth/hook folder i created\nuseAuthHook. js i wrote all login and register login there and for \nhandling for i used react-hook-fom and in when user login then \npass login data to loginUserApi function pass request to dummyjson\napi then they return login user all predifined user data. also i crated\nredux store i inside auth/state folder i created authslice inside \nthat i created two reducers/actions addUser and remover user\nand when user login then i dispatch adduser inside reponce that give \napi of user data. when refresh the web site our logged user data \nnever loss so i used hydrate concept. for that, first when post\napi return responce then i store accessToken inside local store and\nthen i craete hydrate function inside hadrate function called api to\nget logged user using previous logged use access stoken this is code\n \nexport const hydrateUser = async() => {\n  const token = localStorage.getItem(\"accessToken\");\n  try {\n    let res = await api.get(\"/auth/me\", {\n      headers: {\n        Authorization: `Bearer ${token}`, // Pass JWT via Authorization header\n      },\n    });\n    return res.data;\n  } catch (error) {\n    console.log(\"responce hydrate error: \", error);\n  }\n};\n\n\nnow i created routes folder inside src folder and also create authProted.jsx\nand mainprotected.jsx for protecting authlayout and mainLayout \naccording to user logged or log out. \nfor that i used useSelect() and get user state is null or user is there. \nthis is mainprotected code. \nimport React from \"react\";\nimport { useSelector } from \"react-redux\";\nimport { Navigate, Outlet } from \"react-router\";\n\nconst MainProtected = () => {\n  const { user, isLoading } = useSelector((store) => store.auth);\n\n  if(isLoading) return <h1>Loading State...</h1>;\n\n  if (!user) {\n    return <Navigate to={\"/\"} />;\n  }\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      <Outlet />\n    </div>\n  );\n};\n\nexport default MainProtected;\n\nand this is authProtected code:\n\nimport React from 'react';\nimport { useSelector } from 'react-redux';\nimport { Navigate, Outlet } from 'react-router';\n\nconst AuthProtected = () => {\n    const {user, isLoading} = useSelector((store) => store.auth);\n    if (isLoading) return <h1>Loading State...</h1>\n    if (user) {\n        return <Navigate to={\"/main\"} />\n    }\n  return (\n    <div>\n      <Outlet/>\n    </div>\n  );\n}\n\nexport default AuthProtected;\n\n\nand this is approutes.jsx code:\n\nimport React, { Children, useEffect } from \"react\";\nimport { createBrowserRouter, RouterProvider } from \"react-router\";\nimport AuthLayout from \"../app/layouts/AuthLayout\";\nimport MainLayout from \"../app/layouts/MainLayout\";\nimport AuthProtected from \"./protected/AuthProtected\";\nimport RegisterPage from \"../features/auth/ui/pages/RegisterPage\";\nimport MainProtected from \"./protected/MainProtected\";\nimport HomePage from \"../shared/ui/pages/HomePage\";\nimport ProductPage from \"../features/products/ui/pages/ProductPage\";\nimport AboutPage from \"../shared/ui/pages/AboutPage\";\nimport OrderPage from \"../features/orders/ui/pages/OrderPage\";\nimport CartPage from \"../features/cart/ui/pages/CartPage\";\nimport LoginPage from \"../features/auth/ui/pages/LoginPage\";\nimport { useDispatch } from \"react-redux\";\nimport { addUser } from \"../features/auth/state/authSlice\";\nimport { hydrateUser } from \"../features/auth/api/authApi\";\n\nconst AppRoutes = () => {\n  const disptach = useDispatch();\n\n  useEffect(() => {\n    (async () => {\n      try {\n        let responce = await hydrateUser();\n        disptach(addUser(responce));\n      } catch (error) {\n        console.log(\"error in hydration: \", error);\n      }\n    })();\n  }, []);\n\n  let router = createBrowserRouter([\n    {\n      path: \"/\",\n      element: <AuthProtected />,\n      children: [\n        {\n          path: \"\",\n          element: <AuthLayout />,\n          children: [\n            {\n              path: \"\",\n              element: <LoginPage />,\n            },\n            {\n              path: \"register\",\n              element: <RegisterPage />,\n            },\n          ],\n        },\n      ],\n    },\n    {\n      path: \"/main\",\n      element: <MainProtected />,\n      children: [\n        {\n          path: \"\",\n          element: <MainLayout />,\n          children: [\n            {\n              path: \"\",\n              element: <HomePage />,\n            },\n            {\n              path: \"product\",\n              element: <ProductPage />,\n            },\n            {\n              path: \"about\",\n              element: <AboutPage />,\n            },\n\n            {\n              path: \"cart\",\n              element: <CartPage />,\n            },\n            {\n              path: \"orders\",\n              element: <OrderPage />,\n            },\n          ],\n        },\n      ],\n    },\n  ]);\n  return <RouterProvider router={router} />;\n};\n\nexport default AppRoutes;\n\n",
